evals.prompt:
Review this worker code for concurrency defects:

```javascript
// Path A: called from the queue consumer
function reserveThenCharge(order) {
  inventoryLock.acquire();
  billingLock.acquire();
  try { /* reserve stock, then charge card */ } finally {
    billingLock.release();
    inventoryLock.release();
  }
}

// Path B: called from the refund webhook handler
function refundThenRelease(order) {
  billingLock.acquire();
  inventoryLock.acquire();
  try { /* refund card, then release stock */ } finally {
    inventoryLock.release();
    billingLock.release();
  }
}
```
Both paths can run concurrently. What is wrong, and what is the fix?
